            <ArticleTitle>Principles of restoring function and sensorimotor control in patients with shoulder dysfunction.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>507-19, x</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.csm.2008.02.003</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This article reviews the basic principles of restoring sensorimotor (SMS) function and evidence-based outcome assessments and describes their integration into treating patients who have shoulder dysfunction. When integrated clinically, the principles of restoring SMS function act in synergy with those of functional outcome-based practices.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
